{
  "run_id": "PMC11643467__broad__pcd_D_o3mini__s1",
  "auditor": "trapi:gpt-5.6-sol_2026-07-09",
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "Adding 1–2 at.% Ti to CoCrFeMnNi and applying an optimized heat treatment will produce a uniform nanoscale dispersion of Ti-rich precipitates.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10744552::web::002::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "A solution treatment near 1150°C with an adjusted cooling rate can control precipitate size and distribution in the Ti-modified CoCrFeMnNi alloy.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10744552::web::002::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Controlled cooling will avoid coarse precipitate growth.",
      "field": "conditions",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10744552::web::002::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The resulting Ti-rich precipitates will be carbides and oxides located both at grain boundaries and within grains.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Ti will react with residual carbon and oxygen during processing to form stable carbide and oxide precipitates.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Ti-rich carbide and oxide precipitates will impede dislocation motion.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC8510135::web::026::4_2_characterization_of_the_rhea_bulks"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The precipitate dispersion will increase the yield strength of Ti-modified CoCrFeMnNi.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10744552::web::002::1_introduction",
        "PMC8510135::web::026::4_2_characterization_of_the_rhea_bulks"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The precipitate dispersion will reduce the room-temperature creep rate of Ti-modified CoCrFeMnNi.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Ti-rich precipitates at grain boundaries will promote formation of protective oxide films.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Protective oxide-film formation associated with the precipitates will enhance corrosion resistance.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10744552::web::002::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Relative to CoCrFeMnNi without Ti, the Ti-modified alloy will have higher yield strength.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10744552::web::002::1_introduction",
        "PMC8510135::web::026::4_2_characterization_of_the_rhea_bulks"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Relative to CoCrFeMnNi without Ti, the Ti-modified alloy will have a lower room-temperature creep rate.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Relative to CoCrFeMnNi without Ti, the Ti-modified alloy will exhibit improved corrosion passivation.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10744552::web::002::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The magnitude of the strength, creep, and corrosion improvements will depend on precipitate morphology.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10744552::web::002::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Performance improvements will be less pronounced if the precipitates coarsen or become non-uniform.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10744552::web::002::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Carbides and oxides can strengthen high-entropy alloys and contribute to their stability and wear resistance.",
      "field": "prior evidence",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC8510135::web::026::4_2_characterization_of_the_rhea_bulks"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Precipitation-treatment control can regulate precipitate size and distribution and thereby alter mechanical and corrosion properties.",
      "field": "prior evidence",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10744552::web::002::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    }
  ],
